Simple3JointArm is a StateToGeometry child that is designed for a robotic arm with three
independently actuated rotary joints connected by two fixed size links (conventional yaw-pitch-pitch arm)

Simple3JointArmEffector is designed for the visualizing of this model in 3 dimensions

the 3 independently actuated rotary joints consist of:
    1. Rotation around the central vertical axis (base)
    2. Controls the angle between the first link and the base (shoulder)
    3. Placed between the first and second link (elbow)

these 3 joints give end effector access to 3 dimensional space



this model uses radians and capsule links


base angle of 0 = x+
base angle of 0.5PI = y
base angle of PI = x-
base angle of 1.5PI = y-

shoulder angle of 0 = 0 horizontal
shoulder angle of 0.5PI = vertical up
shoulder angle of PI = horizontal backwards
shoulder angle of 1.5PI = vertical down

elbow angle of 0 = aligned with previous link
elbow angle of 0.5PI = a 90 to the previous link
elbow angle of PI = next to previous link
elbow angle of 1.5PI = a 90 to the previous link